WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.630
- Okay, welcome, everybody.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.140
I'm Maurice Samuels.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:11.700
And it's my great pleasure
to welcome you here

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.200
this afternoon to the last talk

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:19.200
in this year's Benjamin and
Barbara Zucker lecture series.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.830
Today's speaker David de Jong

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:24.630
is a correspondent in the Middle East

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:27.600
where he writes for the
Dutch Financial Daily,

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.700
among other publications.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.930
For the research and writing
of "Nazi Billionaires,"

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.940
he reported from Berlin for four years.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:40.650
Before that de Jong was a
reporter at Bloomberg News

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:43.630
in New York where he
wrote about hidden wealth

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:47.570
and in Amsterdam where he
wrote about European banking

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:48.830
and finance.

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:51.940
His work has also appeared
in the New York Times,

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:55.700
the Wall Street Journal and
Bloomberg Business Week.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.530
De Jong was born and raised in Amsterdam

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:01.327
and currently lives in Tel Aviv.

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:05.000
"Nazi Billionaires" is his first book.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.379
And many of you probably
saw his really fantastic,

00:01:09.379 --> 00:01:13.420
hard hitting op-ed in the
New York Times last week.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:16.658
So hopefully we'll have time
to discuss that as well.

00:01:16.658 --> 00:01:21.658
So a word first about how
things will work today,

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:24.080
David will speak for about 40 minutes,

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.150
and then we will open it up to
questions from the audience.

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:32.070
Please submit your questions
using the Q&amp;A function

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:34.650
at the bottom of your screen.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.640
We won't be able to see or hear you,

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:40.780
but you can submit questions
at any time during the talk

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:45.555
using the Q&amp;A function, and
I will relay them to David.

00:01:45.555 --> 00:01:49.470
So, yeah, so without further ado,

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:52.060
it's really a great
pleasure to see David again,

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:55.853
who I got to know a little
bit in Berlin last year,

00:01:55.853 --> 00:01:58.400
and really excited to
hear more about this book,

00:01:58.400 --> 00:01:59.820
which I've just been reading.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:02.820
And I have to say is
just a fantastic read.

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:04.723
In addition to being about, you know,

00:02:04.723 --> 00:02:06.660
a completely fascinating subject matter,

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.580
it's really well written.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:09.710
It reads like a novel,

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:11.780
so I highly recommend it to everyone.

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:15.320
All right, now I will
hand it over to David.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:18.843
- Thank you so much, Maurie,
for that kind introduction,

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:24.407
I am going to be talking
about the families in my book,

00:02:24.407 --> 00:02:27.190
who I think, the five families
I write about in my book,

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:30.320
who I think very much,
very well represent,

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:33.669
or their patriarchs at
least very well represent

00:02:33.669 --> 00:02:36.740
this kind of, you know,
German big business

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:39.050
or at least an overview
of German big business

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:42.650
because these families were
then and are still today

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:46.093
Germany's most prominent
business dynasties.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:50.080
And I wanna start it off with,

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:55.080
I'm gonna try and condense
a century from 1919 to 2019

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:57.590
in about 40 minutes.

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:00.350
So I'll be zigzagging
through the five families,

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:04.290
but I'll start off with the
main family, the Quandt dynasty,

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:09.290
whose heirs today control BMW,
at least two of the heirs.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:13.220
It's still Germany's
wealthiest family today,

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:18.220
and their patriarch Gunther
Quandt loses his wife, Antonia,

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:23.180
in the Spanish flu of 1918.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:28.180
And in the fall of, pardon
in the spring of 1919,

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.760
he takes a night train
from Berlin to Kassel

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:36.923
in the center of Germany,

00:03:37.896 --> 00:03:41.540
and he meets a, well,
she's not even a woman yet.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:44.100
She's a girl, a 17 year old girl

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.360
called Magda Friedlander.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:50.410
Magda Friedlander, who just
came out of a relationship

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:55.410
with a Jewish student
named Chaim Arlozorov

00:03:56.156 --> 00:04:00.320
who later becomes a very
well known Zionist in Israel

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:05.320
and is shot dead under very
mysterious circumstances in 1933

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:07.390
on the beach of Tel Aviv.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:09.913
She comes out of a
relationship with Arlozorov

00:04:12.056 --> 00:04:14.330
when she takes that night train in Easter,

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:17.230
in the Easter weekend of 1919,

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:18.680
and she meets Gunther Quandt.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:24.720
Magda Friedlander is the,
her stepfather is Jewish,

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:27.280
and she's taken on his last name.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:32.280
Ritschel Friedlander, but
she was baptized Catholic

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:37.400
and raised Catholic, and
she meets Gunter Quandt,

00:04:37.997 --> 00:04:41.960
and they go and they, and
Gunther Quandt was 20 years older

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:45.510
than she is, is completely
enamored with her.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:50.510
And when Magda gets out at
her stop in central Germany

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:56.180
and goes to the boarding
school where she is.

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:58.130
You know, he finds her address,

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:01.330
and he writes to her that very night

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:03.800
when he arrives at his destination,

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:07.040
and he takes her out on a
date and within three dates,

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.135
he proposes to her.

00:05:09.135 --> 00:05:13.390
Gunther has two sons
from his first marriage.

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:16.980
And he proposes to her, and
she, after long consider,

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:21.240
or after, yeah, some
consideration, she says, yes,

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:24.240
and they get married, or she says, yes,

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:25.760
and they get engaged.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:30.230
Now, however, to get married,
he has one condition.

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:32.130
Gunther Quandt has one
condition or two conditions,

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:37.130
that she reconverts from
Catholicism back to Protestantism,

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.770
which is his, he's Lutheran.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:44.770
And secondly that she
drops the name Friedlander

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:47.290
before she gets married.

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:51.507
And that she reassumes
her birth name, Ritschel,

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:55.990
which was her biological father's name

00:05:56.920 --> 00:06:01.920
because, you know, of course
from his perspective, you know,

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:04.678
he could never get married,

00:06:04.678 --> 00:06:07.120
Gunther Quandt could never
get married to a woman

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:09.290
who holds a Jewish last name.

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:11.370
And I think that is very much,

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:14.210
that episode where the book
starts, where my book starts

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:18.410
is very much emblematic for
the thinking of the families

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.538
or at least the patriarchs of the families

00:06:20.538 --> 00:06:22.820
I'm writing about.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:26.319
This latent antisemitism,

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:31.319
as opposed to the really
racial antisemitism,

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:34.482
this convinced antisemitism.

00:06:34.482 --> 00:06:37.710
These men I write about are not,

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:40.320
they are not convinced antisemites.

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:44.270
They are, you know, for
the most part Protestants

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:48.900
who, you know, very much a
Lutheran theology, you know,

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:53.900
is, you know, from my
view deeply antisemitic.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:58.921
Also many voters who
voted in the Nazi party,

00:06:58.921 --> 00:07:03.657
there was far higher votes for the NSDAP,

00:07:03.657 --> 00:07:07.018
in the more Protestant parts of Germany

00:07:07.018 --> 00:07:12.018
who saw Hitler really as a
sort of reincarnation to many

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.160
of Martin Luther.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:19.040
So it is really this latent antisemitism

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.360
that is prevalent not only in
the circles of big business,

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:25.077
but I would say unfortunately
for the most part

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:29.030
of Christian German society,

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:34.030
both Protestant and Catholic at that time.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:35.303
Now Gunther Quandt,

00:07:36.397 --> 00:07:37.960
who was already from
a very wealthy family,

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:42.190
a textile family, builds up this empire

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:45.430
during the era of hyperinflation

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:50.430
as does his, well, fellow
industrialist, Friedrich Flick,

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.396
who ends up being

00:07:55.396 --> 00:07:59.814
probably Germany's most
notorious industrialist

00:07:59.814 --> 00:08:02.540
of the 20th century and who
is eventually convicted,

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.980
the only one in of my main characters,

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:07.150
who's eventually convicted at Nuremberg

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:10.023
for war crimes and
crimes against humanity.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:15.480
The two of them separately
start very much profiting

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:20.480
from the era of
hyperinflation in the 1920s.

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:28.070
Gunther Quandt manages
through hyperinflation,

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:30.160
which wiped out most
of the middle classes.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:32.430
But for the speculators of the time,

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:36.495
the stock speculators of the
time was a very profitable era,

00:08:36.495 --> 00:08:41.495
managed to take control of a
global battery factory, AFA,

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:45.210
and a global or a weapons factory,

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:47.253
or a weapons firm called DWM.

00:08:49.364 --> 00:08:50.300
And that is really the groundwork

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:54.180
of the Quandt business
empire that they see,

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:59.180
that they very much profit
from after Hitler seizes power

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:01.130
in 1933.

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:04.883
Now, as for Friedrich Flick,
he parlays a steel company

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:11.470
that he controls into
a steel conglomerate.

00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:15.080
He takes over the United Steelworks

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:18.160
during the hyperinflation era.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:23.160
And it is very interesting to
see how virulent antisemitism

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:29.040
is already leveled against
kind of the Jewish speculators,

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:33.630
of the great Jewish speculators
of that era in Germany,

00:09:35.742 --> 00:09:38.320
where there is this idea of, you know,

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:39.790
they're just speculating.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:44.790
They're, you know, accumulating stocks,

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:48.122
and they're accumulating
controlling interests

00:09:48.122 --> 00:09:53.070
in companies, you know, across the board

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:58.070
of the business spectrum
from industry to textiles

00:10:00.378 --> 00:10:03.950
to batteries to weapons.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:08.950
But these same accusations, you know,

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:14.030
which you still see today
leveled against George Soros,

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:16.510
or the conspiracy theorists do,

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:19.820
you know, you don't see them
leveled against Gunther Quandt

00:10:20.698 --> 00:10:22.498
and Friedrich Flick being, you know,

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:28.103
Protestant parts of the
German establishment.

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:34.550
Now I want to go to 1933
and Hitler seizing power

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:36.313
in Germany.

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:43.920
The quickly codifying of
antisemitic laws in Germany,

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:52.490
you quickly see the main,
well, characters in my book

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:53.913
taking advantage of it.

00:10:58.060 --> 00:11:01.590
Gunther Quandt gets briefly detained

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:06.390
because at this point
in time, his marriage

00:11:07.571 --> 00:11:12.571
to Magda Quandt has dissolved,

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:17.900
and Magda Quandt has on
to become Magda Goebbels.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:21.260
She divorces Gunther Quandt in 1929

00:11:22.287 --> 00:11:27.287
and soon meets Joseph Goebbles
who is then the Reich's,

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:34.910
yeah, the Reich's propaganda
lighter for Berlin,

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:37.040
and is, you know, up and coming

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:41.563
in the then still burgeoning Nazi party.

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:46.383
And they soon become the, you know,

00:11:46.383 --> 00:11:49.253
kind of the most prominent
couple of the Third Reich.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:55.100
And a custody battle ensues.

00:11:55.271 --> 00:11:58.660
Gunther Quandt has two sons
from his first marriage,

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:02.410
Herbert and Hellmut, and two,

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:07.300
and has one son together
with Magda called Harald,

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:12.300
called Harald, and a custody
battle about Harald ensues.

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:16.123
And he is arrested,

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:21.110
which he later purports
is on Goebbels's orders.

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:23.540
He's arrested on May 4th, 1933,

00:12:23.540 --> 00:12:26.180
three days after Gunther
Quandt becomes a member

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:28.380
of the Nazi party.

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:33.380
He spends six weeks in custody,

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:35.440
and then as soon as he gets out,

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:37.333
he first has to go into house arrest.

00:12:38.791 --> 00:12:43.791
He starts firing, you
know, the Jewish members

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:48.730
of his supervisory boards
and executive boards.

00:12:48.730 --> 00:12:50.490
He starts removing them

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:55.490
from his company boards, even
though he says, you know,

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:59.630
he later purports himself to be a victim

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:02.460
of Goebbels and a victim
of the Nazi regime

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:06.140
and as an opponent, even though he becomes

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:09.163
one of the Third Reich's
largest profiteers.

00:13:10.742 --> 00:13:14.876
And he, you know, quickly takes advantage

00:13:14.876 --> 00:13:17.970
of business partners that he had.

00:13:17.970 --> 00:13:20.040
There was a banker named Jacob Goldsmith,

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:24.419
which both Friedrich
Flick and Gunther Quandt

00:13:24.419 --> 00:13:25.720
did a lot of business with and was,

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:29.120
served on their company boards.

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:32.950
He is by both Quandt and
Flick is swiftly removed

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:35.700
from his boards, from their boards.

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:39.750
And, you know, is forced
to flee Nazi Germany.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:42.080
And that is again emblematic also

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:44.400
of the thinking of these men.

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:49.400
They are not convinced
anti-Semites, but they are,

00:13:50.133 --> 00:13:53.360
they are willing to play
along with the Nazi regime

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:57.673
as long as it benefits their
companies, their fortunes,

00:13:59.757 --> 00:14:01.360
and, you know,

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:04.563
they will not do anything that
goes against the rules by,

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:10.550
you know, going the extra mile

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:16.302
to save their Jewish
colleagues or employees

00:14:16.302 --> 00:14:18.663
from persecution.

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:24.190
Now, following the implementation

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:26.873
of the Nuremberg Race Laws
in mid-September 1935,

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:33.310
where of course, the
disenfranchisement of Jewish citizens

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:36.390
in Nazi Germany really ramps up,

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:41.350
you see this concept of Arya,

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:44.390
which later became known as Aryanization,

00:14:44.390 --> 00:14:49.390
really enter into the discourse
for German businessmen.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:56.120
And the concept of
Aryanization was this idea

00:14:57.270 --> 00:15:02.270
of the removal of the Jewish element

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:05.700
from the ownership of an asset,

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:10.650
whether that was a Jewish
owned company, shares, jewelry,

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:15.180
art, real estate, that's where it starts.

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:17.760
And of course, initially
these transactions

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:21.800
still have the veneer of a
regular business transaction

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:27.643
between I would say 1935 to 1937,

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:31.330
but they very soon afterwards

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:36.193
become the outright
expropriation and appropriation

00:15:36.193 --> 00:15:38.850
by the Nazi regime,

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:42.372
as well as the businessman
I'm writing about.

00:15:42.372 --> 00:15:44.450
I mean, I give countless
examples in my book

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:49.450
of Aryanization, but I will give several,

00:15:52.170 --> 00:15:54.910
and the most prominent
one I wanna start with

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:59.910
is the removal of Adolf Rosenberger,

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:04.150
the co-founder of Porsche,
of the Porsche company

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:05.610
by his two,

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:09.387
or the buyout is the correct term

00:16:11.774 --> 00:16:15.500
of Adolf Rosenberger by his
two Porsche company co-founders

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:18.803
Anton Piëch and Ferdinand Porsche.

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:24.597
They, the three of them start
the car design company in 1930

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:30.720
in Stuttgart, and they, you know,

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:35.810
on the day that Adolf Rosenberger
resigns in January 1933,

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:39.433
30th of January, 1933 is also the day

00:16:39.433 --> 00:16:42.620
that Adolf Hitler seizes power in Germany.

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:47.620
He resigns, Rosenberger,
because he is fed up with being,

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:49.700
he's the commercial director of Porsche,

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:53.820
and he's fed up with, you know,
being the financial backer

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:55.200
of the Porsche company,

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:59.660
which is blowing through
money on the expensive designs

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:04.413
of Ferdinand Porsche, the
mercurial car designer

00:17:04.413 --> 00:17:09.413
and whose company, you
know, it's namesake company,

00:17:10.381 --> 00:17:13.200
but Adolf Rosenberger
has 10% of the shares.

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:17.987
He stays on, Adolf Rosenberger
as a Porsche shareholder

00:17:20.587 --> 00:17:22.580
until July 1935,

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:26.890
when he's bought out
of the Porsche company

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:29.710
